cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as follows."
title: "closed-loop-neural-culture-control"
abstract: >-
  Closed-loop validation that a load-bearing control function survives a
  simulated spiking culture substrate on a Unitree G1 humanoid (MuJoCo),
  measured with task-tracking ablations (zero/random/lesion/dead-substrate
  nulls), exact permutation statistics, mutual information and transfer
  entropy, substrate interchangeability (rate-code and Izhikevich), terrain
  outcomes, and an explicit authority/latency boundary. Companion manuscript
  under paper/.
keywords:
  - neuromorphic computing
  - spiking neural networks
  - closed-loop control
  - humanoid locomotion
  - mutual information
  - transfer entropy
  - falsification
license: MIT
